on-arrival: gaza_war_2023_done = 1; gaza_chain_stage = 1; gaza_last_position = "No position yet"; foreign_pressure += 2; news_headline = "The war in Gaza forces Lewica to choose a public line"

= October 2023 — After 7 October

Hamas's 7 October attack kills about 1,200 people in Israel and takes roughly
250 hostages. Israel answers with a siege and air campaign in Gaza. Polish
citizens are being evacuated while demonstrations for Israel and Palestine
begin to face one another in Warsaw.

Razem's national board condemns Hamas's attack and says it cannot justify
collective punishment of Palestinian civilians. The old SLD organisation
warns that a one-sided Palestinian line will estrange institutions and voters
for whom Israeli security and Polish-Jewish relations are inseparable. On the
right, Konfederacja's anti-establishment wing sees an opening against the
foreign-policy consensus.

Silence is also a position now: every interviewer will ask which deaths the
party was unwilling to name.

- @gaza_2023_palestine
- @gaza_2023_israel
- @gaza_2023_neutral

@gaza_2023_palestine
title: Condemn Hamas and demand a ceasefire and Palestinian self-determination
subtitle: Gains anti-war voters and Razem; every other parliamentary relationship cools while the SLD organisation rebels.
on-arrival: konf_relation += 4; ko_relation -= 3; psl_relation -= 3; p2050_relation -= 3; pis_relation -= 3; left_poll += 0.4; left_poll_momentum += 0.15; razem_dissent -= 6; barons_dissent += 4; minority_safety += 1; foreign_policy_responsibility += 2; gaza_stance_score = 1; gaza_last_position = "Ceasefire and Palestinian self-determination"; news_headline = "Lewica condemns Hamas and demands a ceasefire for Gaza"

We name the murdered and abducted Israelis, call Hamas's attack terrorism, and
then refuse the claim that the same words authorise collective punishment.
Lewica demands the release of hostages, immediate humanitarian access, a
ceasefire and a political future for Palestinians outside permanent
occupation.

Razem members hear a recognisably internationalist line and stand down their
internal campaign. The SLD organisation hears a diplomatic bridge being
burned. KO, PiS, PSL and Polska 2050 all find different reasons to call the
statement reckless; Konfederacja alone enjoys the breach in the consensus.
The controversy brings a small polling gain among voters who had stopped
expecting anyone to take the risk.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the ceasefire demand on the events desk

@gaza_2023_israel
title: Stand without qualification behind Israel's war against Hamas
subtitle: Calms the SLD organisation and avoids a fight with the centre, but Razem erupts and Konfederacja turns hostile.
on-arrival: konf_relation -= 5; razem_dissent += 11; barons_dissent -= 5; young_support -= 2; left_atlanticist_dissent -= 2; foreign_policy_responsibility += 1; gaza_stance_score = -1; gaza_last_position = "Unqualified support for Israel's war"; news_headline = "Lewica gives Israel unqualified support for the war against Hamas"

The statement stops after the hostages and Israel's right to destroy Hamas.
It contains no ceasefire demand and no condition tied to civilian casualties
or displacement in Gaza.

The SLD organisation welcomes a line it can defend in every established
foreign-policy forum. Razem does not treat the omission as caution: its members
call it consent to collective punishment and begin organising against the
leadership. Konfederacja attacks the party for falling into line behind another
state. No other party rewards us for saying what it was already saying.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the Israel statement on the events desk

@gaza_2023_neutral
title: Condemn every attack and take no position on a ceasefire
subtitle: Avoids choosing an ally; voters and both internal camps read the missing decision instead.
on-arrival: left_poll -= 0.3; left_poll_momentum -= 0.2; public_trust -= 2; media_capacity -= 1; party_unity -= 2; razem_dissent += 4; barons_dissent += 2; gaza_stance_score = 0; gaza_last_position = "Condemnation without a ceasefire position"; news_headline = "Lewica condemns the violence and declines to say what should stop next"

We mourn civilians, oppose antisemitism and Islamophobia, and omit every verb
that would decide what should happen next. Nobody can accuse the statement of
endorsing a belligerent.

That is its only success. Razem asks why a left party cannot demand a halt to
collective punishment; the SLD organisation asks why it cannot clearly stand
with Israel after a terrorist attack. The press reduces two pages to the
missing word “ceasefire,” and a party that wanted safety instead looks afraid.

- @poland_event_queue: File the non-position

@gaza_wck_2024
