= 1 April 2024 — Damian Soból

Three Israeli strikes hit a World Central Kitchen convoy in Gaza and kill all
seven aid workers travelling in it, including **Damian Soból**, a Polish
humanitarian volunteer from Przemyśl. The vehicles were marked and their route
had been coordinated with the Israeli military.

The government condemns the attack and demands an explanation. For Lewica the
question is sharper than another expression of grief: whether a Polish death
changes the political line chosen in October.

[? if gaza_last_position = "Ceasefire and Palestinian self-determination": We
already demanded a ceasefire. Now the party must decide whether its words
carry an accountability mechanism.?] [? if gaza_last_position = "Unqualified
support for Israel's war": Our October statement gave Israel's campaign no
conditions. A Polish coffin has made that omission impossible to hide.?] [? if
gaza_last_position = "Condemnation without a ceasefire position": October's
non-position survived while the victims were distant. It does not survive a
named Polish volunteer.?]

- @gaza_wck_palestine
- @gaza_wck_israel
- @gaza_wck_neutral

@gaza_wck_palestine
title: Demand an independent investigation, a ceasefire and a review of military cooperation
subtitle: Makes Palestinian civilian protection the test; gains polling and Razem support while every other party relationship falls.
on-arrival: konf_relation += 4; ko_relation -= 2; psl_relation -= 2; p2050_relation -= 2; pis_relation -= 2; left_poll += 0.3; left_poll_momentum += 0.15; razem_dissent -= 5; barons_dissent += 4; public_trust += 1; foreign_policy_responsibility += 3; gaza_stance_score += 1; gaza_last_position = "Accountability, ceasefire and Palestinian civilian protection"; news_headline = "Lewica ties Damian Soból's death to an independent inquiry and a ceasefire"

Lewica demands evidence preservation outside the Israeli chain of command,
Polish participation in the investigation, a humanitarian ceasefire and a
review of every form of military cooperation that could continue without
answers.

It is a party demand, not an order to the Foreign Ministry. The line does,
however, make Damian Soból's death part of the wider protection owed to
Palestinian civilians. Razem rallies to it and a small group of voters rewards
the clarity. The SLD organisation and every other parliamentary party accuse
us of turning a Polish victim into a rupture with Israel; Konfederacja welcomes
the rupture for reasons of its own.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the accountability demand on the events desk

@gaza_wck_israel
title: Accept Israel's internal inquiry and keep the war against Hamas separate
subtitle: Restores calm in the SLD organisation; Razem's dissent jumps and Konfederacja punishes alignment.
on-arrival: konf_relation -= 4; razem_dissent += 10; barons_dissent -= 5; public_trust -= 3; young_support -= 2; foreign_policy_responsibility -= 1; gaza_stance_score -= 1; gaza_last_position = "Israeli inquiry without a ceasefire demand"; news_headline = "Lewica accepts Israel's inquiry and separates the strike from the war"

We call the strike a grave failure, accept the Israeli military's promise to
investigate itself and insist that one unlawful attack cannot decide the case
against Hamas.

The SLD organisation gets the continuity it wanted. Razem gets confirmation
that even a named Polish victim does not produce a red line. Konfederacja again
attacks automatic alignment. KO, PSL, Polska 2050 and PiS have no reason to
move closer: we have joined a position already available without us. The
public cost comes from appearing satisfied before the evidence exists.

- @poland_event_queue: Accept the internal inquiry

@gaza_wck_neutral
title: Demand compensation for Soból's family but refuse a wider judgment on the war
subtitle: Narrows the dispute to one Polish claim; both party camps and a grieving public see evasion.
on-arrival: left_poll -= 0.3; left_poll_momentum -= 0.15; public_trust -= 3; party_unity -= 2; razem_dissent += 3; barons_dissent += 2; foreign_policy_responsibility -= 1; gaza_last_position = "A Polish compensation claim without a war position"; news_headline = "Lewica seeks compensation while refusing to connect the strike to the war"

We demand an apology, compensation and a complete file for Damian Soból's
family, but say nothing about a ceasefire, military cooperation or the safety
of the Palestinian civilians among whom aid workers operate.

The claim is concrete and painfully narrow. Razem calls it nationalism without
solidarity; the SLD organisation calls it an attempt to avoid defending
Israel's war. Voters see a Polish death reduced to paperwork because the party
still cannot decide what the death means.

- @poland_event_queue: File the compensation claim

@gaza_campus_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — The Warsaw campus confrontation tests the same foreign-policy divide through speech, institutional ties and policing, with a genuinely costly procedural middle.
title: Police remove the Palestine protest at Warsaw University
subtitle: Student demands over Gaza collide with university autonomy, protest rights and Jewish safety
