= June 2024 — Gaza reaches the Warsaw campus

Students and staff have camped at the University of Warsaw since 24 May,
demanding disclosure of institutional ties and an end to cooperation they say
supports the occupation of Palestine. On 11 June part of the protest moves
into a university building. The rector calls the occupation unacceptable and
police remove the demonstrators.

The university affirms the constitutional right to protest while defending
its authority over its buildings. Jewish students ask whether Lewica will
distinguish criticism of Israel from antisemitic intimidation; Palestinian
students ask whether that concern will be used to make their families'
experience unspeakable.

The party cannot command the rector or police. It can decide whose demand it
will organise behind and which general rule it will defend.

- @gaza_campus_palestine
- @gaza_campus_israel
- @gaza_campus_neutral

@gaza_campus_palestine
title: Back the students' disclosure demand and suspend complicit institutional ties
subtitle: Supports Palestine and wins young anti-war voters; all other party relations fall and the SLD organisation revolts.
on-arrival: konf_relation += 4; ko_relation -= 2; psl_relation -= 2; p2050_relation -= 2; pis_relation -= 2; left_poll += 0.3; left_poll_momentum += 0.15; razem_dissent -= 5; barons_dissent += 4; young_support += 3; urban_progressive_support += 2; public_trust -= 1; gaza_stance_score += 1; gaza_last_position = "Campus disclosure and suspension of complicit ties"; news_headline = "Lewica backs the Warsaw students' Palestine disclosure campaign"

Lewica joins the demand for a public register of university partnerships and
for suspension where a partner materially supports occupation or violations
of international law. We defend peaceful protest, reject antisemitic speech
and say neither principle cancels the other.

The line wins organisers and closes the Razem argument for now. It also gives
the SLD organisation a new case against the leadership and cools relations
with every other parliamentary party. Konfederacja applauds the breach with
the establishment while attacking the students on almost everything else.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the disclosure demand on the events desk

@gaza_campus_israel
title: Back the removal and reject an institutional boycott of Israel
subtitle: Reassures the SLD organisation; Razem's dissent surges and Konfederacja attacks the establishment line.
on-arrival: konf_relation -= 4; razem_dissent += 10; barons_dissent -= 5; young_support -= 3; urban_progressive_support -= 2; public_trust -= 1; gaza_stance_score -= 1; gaza_last_position = "Removal of the occupation and no Israel boycott"; news_headline = "Lewica backs the removal and rejects an institutional boycott of Israel"

We say a university building cannot be occupied to compel a foreign-policy
test and that Israeli academic institutions cannot be treated as extensions
of their government. The rector was entitled to recover the premises and the
party will not support a boycott.

The SLD organisation welcomes a firm institutional line. Razem hears the
police removal defended and the students' substantive demand dismissed in the
same breath. Konfederacja attacks a left party guarding establishment ties.
The other parties were already close enough to this position that none owes us
anything for adopting it.

- @poland_event_queue: Back the rector's line

@gaza_campus_neutral
title: Defend protest rights, reject the occupation and refuse both blanket boycotts and endorsement
subtitle: A procedural line protects a boundary but satisfies neither camp and costs the party political reach.
on-arrival: constitutional_restraint += 3; minority_safety += 2; party_unity -= 3; left_poll -= 0.2; left_poll_momentum -= 0.1; media_capacity -= 1; razem_dissent += 3; barons_dissent += 2; young_support -= 1; gaza_last_position = "Protest rights without boycott or endorsement"; news_headline = "Lewica defends protest rights but refuses both occupation and boycott politics"

We oppose occupying teaching space and oppose treating peaceful encampment as
a security threat. We demand published, viewpoint-neutral rules for campus
protest and protection against antisemitic and anti-Palestinian harassment,
while refusing either a blanket institutional boycott or a party endorsement
of the encampment.

It is a defensible general rule and a poor coalition. Razem sees the boycott
demand denied, the SLD organisation sees the protesters legitimised, and
students see a party more interested in procedure than in the war that brought
them outside. Neutrality preserves the boundary and spends reach, unity and
polling to do it.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the campus rule

@last_generation_mermaid_2024
# prose-audit: Grade A — The first Ostatnie Pokolenie action makes the climate goal, damage to a Warsaw monument and criminal liability three separate questions rather than one morality switch.
title: Orange paint covers the Warsaw Mermaid
subtitle: Ostatnie Pokolenie makes climate inaction visible by damaging a protected Warsaw monument
