on-arrival: last_generation_mermaid_2024_done = 1; last_generation_chain_stage = 1; climate_policy_pressure += 2; far_right_agenda += 1; news_headline = "Ostatnie Pokolenie pours orange paint over the Warsaw Mermaid"

= 8 March 2024 — Orange on the Mermaid

Two activists from **Ostatnie Pokolenie** pour orange paint over Ludwika
Nitschowa's 1939 Warsaw Mermaid and its fountain on the Vistula boulevards.
They say ordinary appeals have failed and name climate breakdown as the greater
damage. Conservators begin assessing the monument; prosecutors open a case.

The action has forced climate policy onto every bulletin by putting a Warsaw
symbol at risk. Lewica must decide whether that is civil disobedience it will
share, a tactic it will separate from the cause, or vandalism it wants punished.
None of the answers can make the orange image disappear.

- @mermaid_defend
- @mermaid_separate
- @mermaid_condemn

@mermaid_defend
title: Stand beside Ostatnie Pokolenie and defend disruptive civil disobedience
subtitle: Gains young organisers and climate pressure; loses polling, public trust and the SLD organisation.
on-arrival: last_generation_stance = "Defend civil disobedience"; climate_activist_support += 2; climate_policy_pressure += 5; young_support += 4; urban_progressive_support += 3; progressives_dissent -= 4; razem_dissent -= 2; barons_dissent += 5; public_trust -= 3; left_poll -= 0.4; left_poll_momentum -= 0.15; news_headline = "Lewica defends the Mermaid action as climate civil disobedience"

We say the paint is removable and the climate damage is not, then put party
figures beside the activists. Younger organisers hear a party prepared to take
their emergency seriously. The SLD organisation sees its national campaign
made answerable for damage to a Warsaw monument.

The distinction between reversible paint and irreversible warming survives in
our full statement. In public it becomes a shorter proposition: Lewica defended
the people who covered the Mermaid. We gain committed organisers and lose
broader trust and polling.

- @poland_event_queue: Own the defence

@mermaid_separate
title: Condemn the damage and publish the activists' transport demands in full
subtitle: Keeps the climate issue alive, but loses message discipline and irritates both internal camps.
on-arrival: last_generation_stance = "Separate the cause from the tactic"; climate_activist_support += 0; climate_policy_pressure += 3; progressive_credibility += 2; public_trust += 1; party_unity -= 2; media_capacity -= 1; progressives_dissent += 2; barons_dissent += 1; left_poll_momentum -= 0.1; news_headline = "Lewica condemns the paint and republishes Ostatnie Pokolenie's demands"

The first sentence condemns damage to the Mermaid. The second prints the
group's demands for regional public transport and a shift away from motorway
spending, so that every report repeating our rebuke must also say what the
activists asked for.

It is neither silence nor endorsement. Activists accuse us of using their
arrests as a media hook; the SLD organisation asks why vandals received a
policy platform. The cause stays visible while a divided party loses control
of which half of its statement becomes the headline.

- @poland_event_queue: File the divided statement

@mermaid_condemn
title: Call it vandalism and demand restitution through the ordinary criminal case
subtitle: Gains establishment trust and calms the SLD organisation; younger and progressive support falls as climate pressure goes unanswered.
on-arrival: last_generation_stance = "Condemn and prosecute"; climate_activist_support -= 2; public_trust += 2; left_poll += 0.2; barons_dissent -= 3; progressives_dissent += 6; razem_dissent += 3; young_support -= 3; climate_pressure_unmet += 4; climate_policy_pressure += 1; pis_relation += 2; ko_relation += 1; news_headline = "Lewica calls the Mermaid action vandalism and backs restitution"

We defend the right to protest and insist that it does not include damaging a
protected monument. The party backs an ordinary investigation, conservation
costs proved by evidence and restitution if a court finds liability.

The clear line restores some public trust and the SLD organisation relaxes.
Progressive organisers see climate breakdown displaced by a property case, and
younger supporters hear a familiar promise to respect protest only when it is
easy to ignore. The pressure that produced the action remains unanswered.

- @poland_event_queue: Back the ordinary case

