= 15 April 2024 — The bridges

After Prime Minister **[+ prime_minister +]** does not accept its ultimatum, Ostatnie
Pokolenie begins a campaign of blockades on Warsaw bridges. Activists demand
that money planned for new expressways and motorways be redirected to regional
and local rail and buses, together with a nationwide **PLN 50 monthly regional
transport ticket**.

Drivers manoeuvre around people sitting in traffic lanes; police remove and
identify demonstrators. The demands concern transport exclusion far beyond
Warsaw, but the tactic imposes its cost on people trapped in Warsaw now.

[? if last_generation_stance = "Defend civil disobedience": We defended the
Mermaid action as necessary disruption. The group now expects us to mean the
same thing when disruption reaches commuters.?] [? if last_generation_stance =
"Separate the cause from the tactic": We tried to separate the transport case
from the orange paint. The bridge campaign has put them together again.?] [? if
last_generation_stance = "Condemn and prosecute": We backed the ordinary case
over the Mermaid. The activists answer with an action repeated faster than a
court can process it.?]

- @bridges_transport_bill
- @bridges_observers
- @bridges_penalties

@bridges_transport_bill
title: Put both transport demands into a Lewica bill and ask the activists to clear the roads
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Gives the disruption a parliamentary route; strains coalition relations and creates an unfunded promise.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The parliamentary and costing team needs one resource to produce the bill.
