on-arrival: last_generation_wislostrada_2024_done = 1; last_generation_chain_stage = 3; climate_policy_pressure += 4; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "Repeated Wisłostrada blockades bring a promise of decisive government action"

= December 2024 — The Wisłostrada campaign

Ostatnie Pokolenie has returned to the Wisłostrada again and again since 25
November, sometimes re-entering the road after police remove one blockade.
Prime Minister **[+ prime_minister +]** condemns the disruption and promises
decisive action. The group announces an even larger blockade for 13 December
and repeats the same two
transport demands it brought to the bridges in April.

Drivers have threatened and manhandled protesters; protesters have knowingly
returned to a road where the conflict is becoming less controllable. A harsher
response may clear the carriageway without resolving the campaign. Solidarity
may protect protest while asking commuters to absorb its strategy.

Our last position was **[+ last_generation_stance +]**. The next line will be
read as either its consequence or its abandonment.

- @wislostrada_mediate
- @wislostrada_solidarity
- @wislostrada_crackdown

@wislostrada_mediate
title: Offer transport talks, independent safety monitors and a pause in blockades
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Buys a political route at the price of KO relations, an unfunded commitment and SLD anger.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Credible mediation and independent monitors need one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; last_generation_stance = "Transport talks and monitored pause"; climate_activist_support += 1; climate_policy_pressure += 4; climate_pressure_unmet -= 3; constitutional_restraint += 2; public_trust += 1; progressive_credibility += 2; progressives_dissent -= 3; barons_dissent += 3; ko_relation -= 3; budget_promises += 1; last_policy_stage = "Negotiated proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Lewica party mediation"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Lewica offers monitored transport talks in exchange for a pause in blockades"

Lewica offers a public table on the regional ticket and road-to-rail funding,
independent monitors for every removal, and a request—not an injunction—for a
pause while the talks run. Neither the party nor its ministers pretend they can
guarantee a national budget settlement alone.

KO accuses us of undercutting the prime minister after disruption; the SLD
organisation calls the table a reward for escalation. The activists receive no
victory in advance and must decide whether a visible process is worth leaving
the road. We spend organisation, coalition trust and an unfunded commitment to
make the choice real.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the monitored talks on the events desk

@wislostrada_solidarity
title: Oppose the crackdown and stand publicly with the blockade campaign
subtitle: Gains climate organisers and young support; costs polling, public trust, KO relations and the SLD organisation.
on-arrival: last_generation_stance = "Solidarity with the blockade campaign"; climate_activist_support += 2; climate_policy_pressure += 6; young_support += 4; urban_progressive_support += 3; progressives_dissent -= 4; razem_dissent -= 2; barons_dissent += 6; ko_relation -= 4; public_trust -= 3; left_poll -= 0.5; left_poll_momentum -= 0.2; news_headline = "Lewica opposes the crackdown and stands with the Wisłostrada campaign"

Party figures join the roadside solidarity demonstration, demand protection
from attacks by drivers and say repeated disruption is the foreseeable result
of repeatedly ignoring the transport demands.

Ostatnie Pokolenie gains political cover and young organisers move toward us.
KO treats the appearance as a direct challenge to the prime minister; the SLD
organisation treats it as the final surrender of electoral judgment. The
public argument is no longer only about climate or buses. Lewica now owns the
blockade tactic and pays for it in trust and polling.

- @poland_event_queue: Own the solidarity line

@wislostrada_crackdown
title: Back decisive removal, civil damages and escalating sanctions
subtitle: Aligns with the government and calms the SLD organisation; progressive dissent and unmet climate pressure surge.
on-arrival: last_generation_stance = "Decisive removal and civil damages"; climate_activist_support -= 3; public_trust += 2; barons_dissent -= 4; progressives_dissent += 8; razem_dissent += 4; young_support -= 4; climate_pressure_unmet += 6; far_right_agenda += 2; ko_relation += 4; pis_relation += 2; psl_relation += 2; news_headline = "Lewica backs decisive removals and damages against the Wisłostrada campaign"

We support rapid removal from live roads, civil recovery of documented costs
and escalating sanctions for organisers who repeatedly return. We also demand
body-camera evidence and medical access during removals, safeguards that do
not change which side of the confrontation we have joined.

The government receives the cross-party front it wanted and the SLD
organisation settles. Progressive members see the party answering climate
failure with punishment; young supporters leave; the far right learns that
ever-harsher protest law can be normalised through an unpopular target. The
road clears before the underlying pressure does.

- @poland_event_queue: Back decisive removal
